CHAPTER V
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 18
Women and children victims of acts of violence shall receive the following rights: a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to recovery;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling that is prompt, appropriate, comfortable and in accordance with needs;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process;
i. the right to assistance; and - 11 -
j. the right to a sense of security and protection.

Article 2
The protection of women and children from acts of violence is implemented based on the principles of:
a. humanity;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. order and legal certainty;
e. transparency; and
f. protection.

